WHY THIS EXISTS. After the measurement I trimmed three comment blocks in the two repair files, because the
global comment rule asks for intent in as few lines as earn their place and one of my blocks had grown to
ten. A comment change moves the build digest, so the retained after-logs named a build the handed sources no
longer produce. Rather than assert that the difference was comment-only, this log rebuilds the handed sources
and re-runs both seeds. Two independent builds, and every figure is the same.

THE TREE. git archive of the base above into a scratch directory, then the sixteen handed paths copied over
it and nothing else. The only untracked provisioning is two symlinks the build recipe needs and git does not
carry, tools -> the clone's tools (the Spike include and lib the ISA shim compiles against) and .venv, plus
the empty dv/auto_dv/work/runtime/out directory the build writes its latest-pointer into. With the tracked
diff taken against the base, the archive differs from HEAD in exactly the three tracked paths of this hand.

THE BUILD. gen_build.py --build gen_tb --waves --local-cocotb, rc=0, zero compile errors,
sources_sha256 e2492acab5c48ecc92ed18f8bcd1cf5700b2a549798d2b5ee601d16317173a17. The measurement build was
3dd4530832d978cdebe71258f2398a61db4e681f9c88f8ec81e187de23e1b8b7.

